<title>USA: Travelers to put options soon in 401(k)s - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Travelers to put options soon in 401(k)s - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Travelers Group Inc could soon become the first employer to put stock options into its employee 401(k) retirement plans, the Wall Street Journal said in its electronic edition on Friday.</p>
<p>The report said the company was expected to soon receive final approval from the U.S. Labor Department to contribute options on its own stock to employees' 401(k) accounts, starting June 30.</p>
<p>The move by Travelers, which has 60,000 employees, could prompt other companies to explore similar routes because of lower costs and associated tax advantages, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
